    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Verified live: the audit log emitted `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (region `NSW` + fiscal year `26` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn check digit `3`).\n\n**Core identifier**\n- Replaced `CustomerCode` \u2192 **`MemberId`**: `format(region, fy, hash8)` builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` then appends the single Luhn `CHK` over that base's digits; `regionOf` reads the region back as the leading letters before the fiscal-year digits (no separator now).\n- Replaced `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` \u2192 **`AssignOwnerMemberId`**: adds the 2-digit fiscal year from `registrationDate` (already set earlier in the pipeline) to the region+hash.\n- Replaced `DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode` \u2192 **`DeduplicateOwnerMemberId`**: collision handling now applies to the `memberId` (`-<n>` suffix from 2).\n\n**Model & persistence**\n- `Owner`: field `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId` (column `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`), getters/setters renamed, `primaryIdentifier()` now returns the memberId.\n- Renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` in all four DB schemas (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Read model, audit, spec**\n- `OwnerMapper`: removed the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings (memberId auto-maps by name); `locality`/`ownerSegment` now derive the region from `MemberId.regionOf(owner.getMemberId())`. `fiscalYear` is unchanged (same value now embedded in the memberId).\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` + `OwnerCreatedEvent`: audit line and structured event now carry `memberId` (dropped the `membershipNumber` field; event JSON key renamed).\n- `openapi.yml`: removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schemas; added `memberId`; updated `locality`'s description.\n- `owners.POST.yml`: renamed the two pipeline steps/classes.\n- Updated the now-accurate javadoc in `Luhn`, `Hashes`, `FiscalYear`, `Localities`.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test confirms `memberId` starts with `NSW`, contains the SHA-256 HASH8, and that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone.",
