        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive unification that preserves the codebase's existing idioms rather than bolting on a new pattern.\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `MemberId` remains the single co-located definition of the id's format/read-back (`format`/`withSuffix`/`regionOf`), exactly mirroring the old `CustomerCode` and the `IdentityKey` idiom it cites. The CHK/Luhn derivation is folded into `MemberId.format` (over the `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` base), and the `%02d` FY formatting moves there too \u2014 so the Luhn call and FY-padding that used to be scattered across the mapper's `checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` expressions now live in one place. The mapper is left only with the by-name `memberId` mapping and the shared `locality`/`ownerSegment` derivations.\n- **Nothing left dangling / no duplication.** A repo-wide grep finds no surviving `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` references except the intentional \"unifies what used to be\u2026\" note in `MemberId`'s javadoc. The Assign/Deduplicate/YAML step names, the audit line, `OwnerCreatedEvent`, `primaryIdentifier()`, schema columns, and the OpenAPI schema all move in lockstep.\n- **Wiring is coherent.** `AssignOwnerMemberId` newly reads `registrationDate`, and the POST pipeline places the `memberId` step (line 83) after `registrationDate`/`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate` (line 63), matching the class's stated ordering contract; dedup still runs before `save`.\n- **No catch-all growth.** `MemberId` carries the same three responsibilities the removed `CustomerCode` did; `regionOf`'s \"leading letters before the first digit\" scan is the minimal adaptation needed now that the format is separator-free, and it's the right home for that knowledge.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this natural."
